// A NESTED FN IS GENERALIZED OVER ITS CAPTURE. `g` returns `outer`'s `k`, an
// Int, so `g(2) ++ "xyz"` concatenates an Int with a String and the program
// must refuse with E_TypeMismatch. It checks clean and runs (measured
// 2026-09-25): the nested fn's type is generalized over every free variable,
// including the one it shares with `outer`'s frame, so each call
// instantiates `k`'s type afresh.
//
// Retires when a nested binding group generalizes only what its enclosing
// frame cannot reach (Hβ.resolve.reference-is-an-edge).
fn outer(k) = {
  fn g(n) = k
  let a = g(1) + 1
  let b = g(2) ++ "xyz"
  a
}

fn main() = outer(5)
